{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>He ties his foal to the vine.</b> He prophesied concerning the land of Judah that it would flow with wine like a spring; a man of Judah could tie one foal to a vine and load it from a single vine, and one branch — one donkey's colt." "<b>His branch.</b> A long tendril; קוריירא בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>He washes in wine.</b> All this is an expression of abundance of wine." "<b>סותה.</b> It is an expression for a type of garment, and it has no parallel in Scripture." "<b>אסרי.</b> Like אוֹסֵר — patterned after מְקִימִי מֵעָפָר דָּל (Psalms 113), הַיֹּשְׁבִי בַּשָּׁמָיִם (ibid. 123), and likewise בְּנִי אֲתֹנוֹ in the same manner. And Onkelos translated it concerning King Messiah: גֶּפֶן — these are Israel; עִירֹה — this is Jerusalem; שֹׂרֵקָה — Israel, as in ״וְאָנֹכִי נְטַעְתִּיךָ שׂוֹרֵק״ (Jeremiah 2)." "<b>בני אתנו.</b> They shall build His palace — the language of שער האיתון in the book of Ezekiel (Ezekiel 40). And they further rendered it in another rendering: גפן אלו צדיקים; בני אתנו — עבדי אורייתא באולפן, after the name of רכבי אתנות צחרת." "<b>כבס ביין.</b> There shall be fine purple whose dye resembles wine. And צבעונין is the term for סותה — garments a woman wears and entices the male with them to set his eyes upon her; and our Rabbis also interpreted it in the Talmud as the term for incitement of drunkenness in tractate Ketubot (111a). And concerning the wine — should you say it does not satisfy, Scripture says סותה."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French corieere, 'runner/tendril'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:12.266511944Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}